Error [jet.ReadOnlyValueNotOwned]: `.move()` cannot take a value out of a guard
  --> tests/ui/ownership/move_out_of_shared_guard_is_rejected.jet:14:22
    |
 14 |     keep(guard.value.res.move())
    |                      ^^^
 Why: The shared storage keeps owning the guard's payload; a move would leave it without that value while its other guards and its cleanup still use it
 Fix: Copy the value with `.copy()` when it supports copying, or assign a new value through the guard to replace it in place
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0120
